SOLUTIONS={
1:('DIG-01','Group the positive numbers: 101 + 1 + 102 = 204. Subtract 2 to get 202.'),
2:('ALG-02','Remove the winning margin of 2 from the total of 8. The remaining 6 goals split equally, giving 3 to each team. Restore the extra 2 to Mary’s team: she wins 5–3, so her team scored 5.'),
3:('DATA-01','Compare the fraction of each spinner occupied by rabbits. A has 3/8, B has 2/4 = 1/2, C has 1/4, D has 2/6 = 1/3, and E has 1/3. One-half is the largest, so choose B.'),
4:('RATE-01','Convert litres to millilitres first: 1.5 L = 1500 mL. Then divide by the capacity of a can: 1500 ÷ 250 = 6 cans.'),
5:('FRAC-01','Convert the bounds to decimals: 1/5 = 0.20 and 1/4 = 0.25. Of the choices, only 0.21 lies strictly between these values.'),
6:('GEO-03','The minute hand makes a full 360° turn each hour. From 2 pm to 4 pm is two hours, so it turns 2 × 360° = 720°. Ending in the same position does not mean it has turned through zero degrees.'),
7:('GEO-04','Three hexagons meet at every vertex, and each pair shares an edge, so those three need different colours. Thus two colours cannot work. Three do work: repeat three colours along each row and shift the pattern for the next row so that every touching pair differs. The minimum is 3.'),
8:('FRAC-02','One-third takes 30 minutes. Two-thirds remains, so at the same rate the remaining time is 2 × 30 = 60 minutes. The total would be 90 minutes, but the question asks how much longer.'),
9:('SPATIAL-01','The S sentries guard rows 5 and 3 and columns B and D. The only candidates left are A,C,E in rows 1,2,4: nine squares. The T at B2 also guards A1 and C1 among those candidates; its other diagonals are already covered by S. The seven unguarded squares are E1, A2, C2, E2, A4, C4 and E4.'),
10:('ALG-01','Let the width be w, so the length is 3w. After the changes, the sides are 3w − 3 and w + 3. Equate them: 3w − 3 = w + 3, hence w = 3. The original length is 9 m.'),
11:('FRAC-03','Using 80% of the battery took 48 hours. The remaining 20% is one-quarter as much charge, so it should last 48 ÷ 4 = 12 more hours under the stated constant-use assumption.'),
12:('DIV-04','Eight odd scores always add to an even total. The minimum is 8 × 3 = 24 and the maximum is 8 × 9 = 72. Of the choices, only 42 is both even and in this interval. It is achievable, for example with seven 5s and one 7: 35 + 7 = 42.'),
13:('DIV-01','Test each prime below 15: 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13. Doubling and adding one gives 5, 7, 11, 15, 23, 27. The prime results come from 2, 3, 5 and 11, so there are 4 jillyprimes.'),
14:('GEO-02','Subtract the four corner triangles from the 6-by-6 square. Each corner triangle has perpendicular legs 2 and 4, hence area ½ × 2 × 4 = 4. The inner square has area 36 − 4 × 4 = 20 square units.'),
15:('RATE-01','The chicken weighs 1750 g, which is 1750 ÷ 500 = 3.5 lots of 500 g. The weight-dependent cooking time is 3.5 × 30 = 105 minutes. Add the initial 20 minutes once: 125 minutes.'),
16:('DIG-01','The original total is 1 + 2 + ⋯ + 9 = 45. Joining adjacent digits a and b changes a + b to 10a + b, an increase of 9a. To reach 99 requires an increase of 54, so 9a = 54 and a = 6. The joined number is 65.'),
17:('COUNT-06','Choose the repeated side length and require the third side to be shorter than twice it. Repeated 2 permits bases 2 or 3: 2 choices. Repeated 3 permits 2 or 3: 2 choices. Repeated 7 permits all four listed lengths: 4 choices. Repeated 11 also permits all four: 4 choices. Total 2 + 2 + 4 + 4 = 12, with each equilateral triangle counted once.'),
18:('ALG-01','Let there be x one-dollar coins, x + 2 two-dollar coins and y fifty-cent coins. The coin count gives 2x + 2 + y = 20, so y = 18 − 2x. The value equation is x + 2(x + 2) + y/2 = 25. Substitution gives 2x + 13 = 25, so x = 6 and y = 6. Check: 8 two-dollar coins, 6 one-dollar coins and 6 fifty-cent coins total $25.'),
19:('RATE-03','Walking one kilometre takes 15 minutes; cycling one kilometre takes 3 minutes. Cycling saves 12 minutes per kilometre. A saving of 24 minutes therefore corresponds to 24 ÷ 12 = 2 km.'),
20:('SOLID-03','There are five consecutive pairs: 1–2, 2–3, 3–4, 4–5 and 5–6. A cube has only three opposite-face pairs, so at most three of these five pairs can avoid sharing an edge. At least two points must be lost. Put 1 opposite 2, 3 opposite 4, and 5 opposite 6; exactly the other two consecutive pairs share edges. Thus the minimum loss is 2.'),
21:('COUNT-06','Include tilted squares as well as upright ones. There are 5 unit upright squares and no larger upright squares. There are 4 small diamond-shaped squares, each with side vector one step across and one step up. Finally there are 2 larger tilted squares with side vectors one across and two up. Total: 5 + 4 + 2 = 11.'),
22:('ALG-01','Let a be the tile width in the direction of the row and b the other dimension. A single tile gives a + b = 12. Four tiles give 4a + b = 24, because the larger perimeter is 48. Subtract to get 3a = 12, hence a = 4 and b = 8. Fifty tiles form a 200 by 8 cm rectangle, with perimeter 2(200 + 8) = 416 cm.'),
23:('DIG-01','Let the two-digit across entry have digits a and b. Its reverse adds to it to make 11(a + b). The grid shows this sum as a three-digit number with tens digit 2. Among multiples of 11 from 110 to 198, only 121 has tens digit 2. Thus a + b = 121 ÷ 11 = 11. This digit sum is exactly the requested 7 down.'),
24:('SOLID-03','A triangular plane cut clips a corner of the cube, meeting its three perpendicular edges at positive distances a, b and c from the corner. Its three squared side lengths are a²+b², a²+c² and b²+c². Any one is strictly smaller than the sum of the other two, so every angle of the cut triangle is acute. It cannot be right-angled. Equal intercepts do give an equilateral triangle; cuts meeting four, five or six faces can give the other listed shapes.'),
25:('SOLID-01','Count removed cubes without counting intersections twice. One large tunnel removes 3 × 1 × 5 = 15 cubes. The second large tunnel shares 3 of those cubes, so adds 15 − 3 = 12. The small tunnel has 5 cubes, but 3 have already been removed by the large tunnels, so it adds only 2. Total removed: 15 + 12 + 2 = 29.')}
